I was walking my pet dog when I found the enterance to a
Colassal Cave.  We wandered around Level One for a while
but I noticed a sewer rat running towards us.  That was too
disgusting so we ran down the stairs.  In that room there was
a sink and out of its pipes I faintly heard strange music.  I was
thirsty so I crouched down and drank from the faunt.  I
underwent a freakish transformation!  Suddenly I was a green
dragon!  My cloak made a shredding noise and was gone.
I had no idea how to react so I stood there and waited to see
what would happen.  A warhouse appeared and it killed my
dog!  I was furious so I grabbed the horse with my claws and
bit it.  Goodbye stupid horse.  The corpse smelled good so I
ate it and continued exploring.  Now I was in the wide corridors
of some mines and a gnome threw some daggers at me.  He
fell into a spiked pit.  The spikes were poisoned!  The poison
was deadly!  Goodbye gnome, but I may as well pick up these
daggers.  Suddenly I'm human again.  So much for being a
green dragon, must've been something I drank.  Another gnome
sees me and runs toward me.  Suddenly there's a flash of
light and it turns into a mumak!  Crap, I've never even seen a
mumak just a sign at the local zoo that they are on loan to the
Detriot zoo.  So I'm really only guessing that it was a mumak
from the trunk.  I run the bleep away down another set of stairs.
A bit of exploring shows that I am now in a shopping district.
I step into am armor shop and a Mordor orc is already there.
He's got a wand and zaps it.  Lightning!  I run away but I don't
think the shopkeeper survived the process.  The orc emerges
from the door and now instead of the wand he's got a runesword.
I don't like the feel I get from that runesword but I am Burdened
from all the shopping I've been doing.  I'm not willing to drop my
loot and the orc can run faster than I can.  He swings the runesword
named Stormbringer!  It hits.  He swings several times and hits
some more.  If you see DYWY... does it mean you're in the
afterlife and have become an immortal demigod?  Uh, turns out
